<!--
  <sui-studio-chrome> — chrome wrapper for the /studio/* subtree.

  Hub port of `apps/shell/src/components/sui-studio-chrome/sui-studio-chrome.sui`
  (the studio's chrome is one of the components this job ports verbatim so the
  shell's studio layout — `routes/studio/_layout.sui`, also ported verbatim —
  has a real custom element to register for the LAYOUTS table; see
  `apps/hub/routes.gen.ts`'s `{ pathPrefix: '/studio', tag: 'sui-studio-chrome' }`).

  Why a hub-local copy instead of importing the shell's:
  the shell's chrome lives in `apps/shell/src/components/sui-studio-chrome/`,
  an APP folder the deck bundler's component-package-roots walker does not
  scan (apps are not in `package.json#workspaces` for the hub build). The
  hub's bundler would resolve `@sui-tag/sui-studio-chrome` to a no-op empty
  module, the chrome custom element would never register, and `document
  .createElement('sui-studio-chrome')` would yield an `HTMLUnknownElement`
  with no `:host` styles — every studio route's chrome collapses to `display:
  inline` / 0x0 and the page's `.studio-view` height chain has no ancestor
  with a resolved height. Same pattern the prior port-studio job used for
  `sui-studio-rail` (`apps/hub/src/components/sui-studio-rail/`, verbatim .sui
  + a controller with a 4-line port seam).

  Body byte-identical to the shell. Slots:
    route       the route content (filled by the host at navigation time)
    bottom      status bar / footer (unused in the hub; the root layout's
                <ship-app-chrome> owns the bottom chrome layer)

  Layout: flex column; `flex: 1; min-height: 0` so it fills the height its
  parent (ship-app-chrome's .app-main) grants via flex, without growing
  beyond it. The route slot's .main takes the remaining height; the footer
  (flex-shrink: 0) sits below it.
-->

<style>
  :host {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    background: var(--surface-0);
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }
  :host([hidden]) { display: none; }

  .main {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bottom {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>

<main class="main" part="main">
  <slot name="route"></slot>
</main>
<footer class="bottom" part="bottom">
  <slot name="bottom"></slot>
</footer>
